  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "node-express-mongodb static-contract baseline",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "x-basis": "Hand-written from the pinned source bezkoder/node-express-mongodb @ 30851145f343ca374dd1bd69998e63c740fea428, independent of scanner output. Express 4 + Mongoose 6 CommonJS app. Models are defined through a default-exported factory (module.exports = mongoose => { ...; return Model; }) invoked in a namespace module (db.tutorials = require('./tutorial.model.js')(mongoose); module.exports = db) and consumed as db.tutorials. The wire document applies a custom toJSON that strips _id/__v and adds id; timestamps add createdAt/updatedAt. findById/findByIdAndUpdate/findByIdAndRemove resolve null to an explicit 404, so a 200 never carries null. find() returns an array (empty list when no rows). update returns a fixed {message}, not the document. Path :id has no cast validation and an invalid id reaches the catch branch as 500, so the path param stays string."
